# Module 06 – Final AI & ML Project Learning Notes

## 1. What is the project?

The AI-Based Job Scam Risk Detector is a Python application that analyses job-posting text and classifies it as potentially suspicious or lower-risk using a trained machine learning model.

## 2. What problem does the project address?

Fake job postings may mislead job seekers through fraudulent offers, upfront payment requests, or misleading employment information. This project aims to provide an initial risk assessment of job-posting text.

## 3. Which technologies are used?

- Python
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn
- TF-IDF Vectorizer
- Logistic Regression
- Joblib
- Regular Expressions

## 4. What is TF-IDF?

TF-IDF stands for Term Frequency–Inverse Document Frequency. It converts text into numerical features that a machine learning model can process.

## 5. Why is Logistic Regression used?

Logistic Regression is a classification algorithm used to predict a class based on input features. In this project, it classifies job-posting text using TF-IDF features.

## 6. What is the role of the trained model?

The trained model analyses the numerical features generated from the job-posting text and predicts a class based on patterns learned during training.

## 7. What is the purpose of rule-based warnings?

Rule-based checks identify predefined warning patterns, such as requests for registration fees or upfront payments. These checks operate separately from the machine learning model.

## 8. What did I learn from this project?

I learned how to prepare text data, train and evaluate a machine learning model, save and load model components, build a Python application, and document a project using GitHub.

## 9. What are the limitations?

The model may produce false positives or false negatives. Its performance depends on the training data, and its predictions do not guarantee whether a job is genuine or fraudulent.

## 10. What are the future improvements?

Possible improvements include creating a web interface, testing on additional datasets, improving error handling, and adding more robust model evaluation.
